[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61764,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Brenner tumour is a tumour composed of nests of bland transitional/urothelial epithelium set within a dense fibromatous stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61765,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9000/0 Brenner tumour NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61766,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F32.Y &amp; XH5DX3 Other specified benign neoplasm of ovary &amp; Brenner tumour NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61767,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61768,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61769,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours occur in the ovary. Extraovarian Brenner tumours have also been reported {1565384; 2071061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61770,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are usually unilateral ovarian tumours but are occasionally bilateral {5043433; 903146}. Most patients are asymptomatic, and the tumours are typically found incidentally in ovaries removed for other reasons {21897739}. Larger tumours may result in abdominal enlargement or pain {445369}. Occasionally, Brenner tumours with functioning stroma are associated with endocrine symptoms {2649834; 4673027}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61771,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Brenner tumours account for approximately 5% of benign ovarian epithelial tumours in clinical studies {5100396; 2685680}. The majority of these tumours arise in adults in the fifth to seventh decade of life, although they may occur in patients aged &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;years or &gt;&nbsp;80&nbsp;years {5043433; 450368}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61772,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of these tumours is not well understood {195239; 18976011; 7448700; 445369}. Some may be derived from Walthard rests, which are nests of metaplastic transitional epithelium in paratubal tissue {24012099}. The rare cases associated with a teratoma may originate from germ cells {4366206; 4367229}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61773,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Walthard nests have been described in association with ovarian mucinous tumours and Brenner tumours {18976011}. Mutations in a variety of genes occur at a low frequency in these tumours {9506354; 28639280}. <em>MYC</em> amplification has been reported {26797085}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61774,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most Brenner tumours are small (&lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;cm), and only rare examples are &gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;cm in dimension {21594602}. Brenner tumours are solid, well-circumscribed nodules with a firm rubbery consistency. The cut surface is greyish-white or yellow and can be calcified. Small cysts are common, and in rare cases the tumour can be predominantly cystic {12649675}. One&nbsp;quarter of Brenner tumours are associated with other tumour types, with mucinous being the most common {11781528; 15482570}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61775,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Brenner tumours are typically composed of small oval to irregular nests of bland transitional/urothelial epithelium in dense fibromatous stroma. The nests often show microcystic spaces containing eosinophilic or mucinous material. These lumina may be lined by transitional, mucinous, ciliated, or cuboidal cells. Mitotic activity is low. Mucinous metaplasia within the lesion is not uncommon {4005815}, and when Brenner tumours are associated with mucinous neoplasms, the mucinous component is usually a cystadenoma. Focal or extensive calcification is frequently seen, and the stroma can be hyalinized.</p>\r\n<h5><em>Immunohistochemistry</em></h5>\r\n<p>Brenner tumours express GATA3, CK7, p63, S100P, AR, uroplakin, and thrombomodulin, but they do not express (or only focally express) CK20 {19092634; 11253121; 2744751; 25281026; 22198845}. PAX8, ER, and PR are typically negative {26095692; 25596159; 25281026}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-02T17:52:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61776,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cells are uniform, with elongated oval nuclei, occasional nuclear grooves, and fine chromatin. Nucleoli can be present. There should not be significant epithelial atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61777,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61778,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tumours with nests of bland transitional/urothelial epithelium set within fibromatous stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:54:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
